In article <31882@ogicse.ogi.edu> noel@ogicse.cse.ogi.edu (Mike Noel) writes:
>A while back during one of the games I was playing I got a message
>that a cave spider jumped out of my pack.  Sure enough, there was a
>cave spider next to me.  I killed it and a few minutes later another
>jumped out.  Where did these guys come from?

Hmmmm.  Could it be that perhaps you had (several turns earlier) picked up
several eggs?  It is a well known fact that various dungeon inhabitants
propagate their kind by laying eggs.  Most of the nethack denizens seem
to be bad parents, and just leave their eggs lying around.  After the
required incubation period, they hatch regardless of whether they are
still on the dungeon floor, or travelling around to see the world in some
hapless adventurer's pack.  :-)

